A||N||6||fropuff||For the paint guys..||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||08-09-2001||12:36 AM||||Hey there.  I just got my 86 GT's new front fascia and ground effects painted, and I've decided that it needs a total buff job.  I want to do it myself, so I can do it right.  I'd first wetsand (not the whole thing; just certain areas) with 1500/2000 grit.  I wetsanded and buffed it last year, so I know how much to sand, so I don't go through.  Then I'd buff the whole thing.  I have a Craftsman 9" electric buffer, and I'm wondering what kind of compound I should use to buff it.  I've heard that a compound be 3M is good; it's a gritty kind.  Thanks for any help.  Have a good one!    <BR><P>------------------<BR>Fiero:  If it ain't broke, it's on fire.  If it ain't on fire, it's broke.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-09-2001||12:40 AM||||Roger??? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Did you see this one? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008496.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008496.html</A> <P><BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000002||fropuff||08-09-2001||12:42 AM||||I was going to specify, but someone else might know too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  DXR: what kind of compound did you use on your red Fiero?  Looks sweet!  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||08-09-2001||12:52 AM||||I guess this is real time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Man the 3M is the best!!!! that red car looked PINK when I got it and had some bad spots. I have a DeWalt adjustable speed polisher and used a wool pad it worked very well. I may go over it one more time. I have not put any wax on the car yet?<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=13270947&p=52062866&Sequence=1&res=high"> <P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||fropuff||08-09-2001||12:55 AM||||One more question..did you use just the 3M stuff, or did you use another product to finish?  Thanks again!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-09-2001||08:47 AM||||3M superduty at auto paint stores, not parts stores.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||08-09-2001||09:19 AM||||3M has a system that uses velcro pads on your air sander.  Paper is 1200, 1500 grit...much faster than hand sanding...incredible results.  Don't worry, I've never burned through edges if the paint, the paper velcros on a foam pad.<P>Then I usually use...(in this order)<P>3M Microfinishing Compound<BR>Liquid Ebony<BR>3M Swirl mark Remover, if needed.<BR>Wax<P>Joe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
